-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS FILE IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is NOT an open-source licence. It is a statement of the position that already
applies, written down so that nobody has to guess.

A repository with no LICENSE file is not "free to use". Under the Berne Convention and
the copyright law of every jurisdiction that implements it, an original work is
protected from the moment it is fixed in a tangible form, with no registration, no
notice, and no ceremony required. The default is that all rights are reserved and no
licence is granted to anyone. Publishing the source on a public host does not change
that; it makes the work readable, not reusable.

So this file grants nothing that was not already granted, and removes nothing that was
not already withheld. What it adds is clarity. In the absence of an explicit statement,
a reader is left to infer intent from the fact of publication, and reasonable people
infer wrongly in both directions — some assume public means permissive, others assume
the omission is deliberate hostility. Neither is true here.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE POSITION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. All rights in this work are reserved by the copyright holder named above.

2. No licence, express or implied, is granted to any person to use, copy, modify,
   merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell copies of this work, or to create
   derivative works from it, except as separately agreed in writing with the copyright
   holder.

3. Viewing the source, cloning the repository, and the operations GitHub's own terms of
   service permit for public repositories (viewing and forking within the platform) are
   not affected by this notice, because they are governed by that agreement rather than
   by this one.

4. This work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
   including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
   particular purpose, and non-infringement. In no event shall the copyright holder be
   liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising from, out of, or in
   connection with this work or its use.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THE LICENCE IS NOT SET
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This code is derived from work produced in the course of employment. The copyright in
it therefore does not belong to the individual contributors, and choosing a licence is
not a decision an engineer, a maintainer, or an automated process is entitled to make on
the owner's behalf. Committing an MIT or Apache-2.0 file here because it is the
customary thing to do in a public repository would be an unauthorised grant of somebody
else's property.

The choice is pending. It requires a decision from whoever is responsible for the
organisation's intellectual property — in practice, legal counsel or the equivalent
delegated authority — and it should consider at least:

  - whether third-party contributions are wanted, and under what contributor agreement;
  - which permissive or copyleft terms are acceptable for a work that will be cloned
    into other projects, which is this repository's entire purpose;
  - patent grants, which differ materially between MIT and Apache-2.0;
  - whether trademark and branding need separate treatment from the code;
  - the licences of the dependencies this work already carries.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT TO DO WITH THIS FILE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

When the decision is made, REPLACE this file entirely with the chosen licence text,
carrying the correct copyright line. Do not append the new licence beneath this notice
and do not keep both: two licence statements in one file is the ambiguity this file
exists to remove.

At the same time, update:

  - README.md            — the "Licence" section and the licence badge
  - src/frontend/package.json — the `license` field
  - CONTRIBUTING.md      — the note about which terms contributions are accepted under

Until then, if you want to use any part of this work, ask. A written grant from the
copyright holder is the only thing that changes the position stated above, and asking is
usually quick.

